From 736d3d634224f5cfe53f4a411ad2747e8d7f1453 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 21:28:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07993/11362] [outer-loop] per-level reset attribution: three
 named units, two reconciling accountings, 10 mutations proved

Lane 1's Change 1 (cumulative reset checkpoints) landed in e871f32be. This is Changes 2 and 3
of its spec plus the review finding it filed against Change 1.

THE DEFECT. The gateway charges a RESET one action (scorecard.py:701-704 inc_reset_count does
`resets += 1` AND `actions += 1`), the per-level score is min((baseline/charged)^2*100, 115), and
the per-level denominator is a DIFFERENCE of cumulative charged counts (:479). So a whole-run
`n_resets` cannot be apportioned across levels after the fact -- recording only the total leaves
every per-level number individually unknowable while still looking instrumented.

MEASURED, and it is not a small correction. vc33 at three seeds carries 13 / 9 / 12 total resets
but 1 / 6 / 12 that actually COST score. The total spans 1.44x; the costly share spans 12x; and
the cell with the MOST total resets has the FEWEST costly ones -- so ordering by the whole-run
total MIS-RANKS the quantity that matters. Relative score loss on the 7 won cells: median 4.5%,
max 12.0%.

WHAT LANDED
  - run_game records each inter-level-up SPAN in ALL THREE units (offline_actions excludes resets,
    frames includes them, gateway_charged is what the scorer bills), with multi-level jumps closing
    one span per level (first carries the cost, rest zero) mirroring the gateway's actions_by_level.
  - Two independent accountings, cross-checked: in-loop accumulators vs an independent
    frame_sequence re-derivation vs the whole-run counters. `discrepancies` is an empty LIST when
    clean and NAMES the failing check otherwise. Reconciles on 18/18 cells.
  - _navigation_diagnostics stops narrowing 24 keys to 2. It was discarding
    reset_replay_fallbacks / navigation_attempts / the exact-vs-partial-vs-similarity split -- the
    exact fields that classify a reset, which is why the prior analysis had to re-run the agent
    live instead of reading rows. Legacy keys retained and typed.
  - Lever-harness row projects the spans and the nav counters under a `navdiag_` prefix. The row's
    existing `n_nav_actions` means NON-CLICK ACTIONS (one vc33 row reads 0 while carrying 115
    resets), so a distinct prefix was mandatory.
  - REVIEW FINDING FIXED (filed by lane 1 against Change 1): eff_gateway defaulted to 0.0, and
    efficiency_optimism_vs_gateway is eff - eff_gateway, so a game exposing no baselines silently
    reported the FULL value of eff as optimism -- "100% optimistic", the most alarming reading
    available -- precisely when nothing was measured. Now None + an explicit error string.

PURE ADDITION, PROVEN NOT ASSERTED
  - Byte-identical trajectory fingerprint (ordered moves + level sequence, SHA-256) for vc33 and
    lp85 at seed 20260724, before vs after the diff.
  - All 5 registered artifacts that declare the edited files as dependencies were REBUILT and
    diffed: 0 number-bearing diffs, including the analyser over the 1401-cell / 2.54-hour sweep.
    Only git_head moved. (artifact-freshness-lint correctly refused until this was done, and
    correctly demanded its own trigger regex cover the new dependency.)
  - Third cross-check: my differenced spans equal lane 1's independently-written cumulative
    checkpoints, differenced, on 9/9 overlapping cells.

TESTS. 10 tests, 10 mutations applied and proved caught (bar was 7): whole-run total substituted
for per-span; gateway_charged dropping the reset charge; cumulative-instead-of-differenced spans;
forced `reconciles` gate; a jump closing one span instead of k; attribution guarded behind a
level-up so the crash path nulls; channel-2 made vacuous; nav narrowed to 2 keys; a dead nav
channel emitting bare zeros without the flag; eff_gateway back to 0.0.

SCOPE AND POWER, hoisted beside the verdict rather than buried: 18 cells / 6 games / 3 seeds at
ONE budget with the LLM OFF. Only 7 cells won a level and attribution exists only where a level-up
does -- sc25/dc22/r11l never levelled at budget 400. The proxy-failure witness rests on ONE game
(vc33, 3 seeds); a 3-point support cannot reach p<0.05, so the claim is EXISTENTIAL ("a cell with
more total resets can have fewer costly ones") and settled by one counterexample, NOT a correlation
estimate. tu93 is seed-INVARIANT here, so its three cells are one measurement. The plan-execution
reset (arc_competition_agent.py:5314) fires only with induction ON and remains UNMEASURED.

Nothing submitted. MAX_ACTIONS and every SUBMITTED_* flag untouched. No historical artifact's
recorded numbers rewritten -- the gateway-charged figures are NEW fields beside preserved originals.

Spec: REQ-ARC-WMTE-5985 + 9 SCENARIOs.

